{"id":"eeaf317b-0ddd-4e28-8b3d-46f98e5261a9","object":"chat.completion","created":1785031959,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be dict\\\")\\n    for key in ['text', 'passes', 'max_rounds']:\\n        if key not in case:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing key: {key}\\\")\\n    text = case['text']\\n    passes = case['passes']\\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\\n    if not isinstance(passes, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"passes must be list\\\")\\n    for p in passes:\\n        if not isinstance(p, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each pass must be dict\\\")\\n        for k in ['name', 'old', 'new']:\\n            if k not in p:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Pass missing key: {k}\\\")\\n    current = text\\n    applications = []\\n    for round_idx in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed_in_round = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p['old']\\n            new = p['new']\\n            if old in current:\\n                current = current.replace(old, new, 1)\\n                applications.append(p['name'])\\n                changed_in_round = True\\n        if not changed_in_round:\\n            return {\\n                \\\"applications\\\": applications,\\n                \\\"fixed_point\\\": True,\\n                \\\"text\\\": current\\n            }\\n    return {\\n        \\\"applications\\\": applications,\\n        \\\"fixed_point\\\": False,\\n        \\\"text\\\": current\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement the solve function according to the described task. The task is about a pass scheduler that applies a sequence of transformation passes to a text. The goal is to apply passes in order, each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep, record passes that change the artifact, repeat full sweeps until no change or rounds exhausted, then return the final text, list of pass names that were applied, and whether it reached fixed point.\n\nWe have input case payload with:\n- text: initial string\n- passes: list of objects with name, old, new (substitution: replace old with new)\n- max_rounds: integer maximum number of sweeps/rounds (each round is one full sweep over all passes in order)\n\nWe need to implement solve(case) that returns dict with keys: \"applications\" (list of strings, names of passes that were applied in order), \"fixed_point\" (boolean), \"text\" (final string).\n\nImportant: Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep. So in each sweep, for each pass in order, we check if the current text contains the \"old\" string. If yes, we perform ONE replacement (the first occurrence? Probably the first occurrence, but not specified; we can assume we replace the first occurrence of old with new). Then record that pass name in applications for that round. Continue to next pass. After finishing all passes, if any pass was applied in that round, we continue to next round; otherwise we have reached fixed point. Also stop if round count reaches max_rounds (inclusive? The description: \"Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed.\" So we stop when either no change in a sweep (fixed point) or after max_rounds sweeps. We need to check if after max_rounds a change occurred? The fixed_point boolean indicates whether we ended because no change occurred. So after loop, if we finished because no change in last sweep, fixed_point=True; else if we stopped because max_rounds reached, fixed_point=False.\n\nBut careful: The payload example shows max_rounds=8. We need to respect that.\n\nAlso note: The \"passes\" are registered in order. The \"first eligible rewrite per sweep\" likely means for each pass in a sweep, we perform at most one substitution. So we replace the first occurrence of old with new in the current text. Use str.replace(old, new, 1) to replace only first occurrence.\n\nWe must not mutate input. We'll make a copy of text.\n\nEdge cases: If pass's old string not found, no change.\n\nWe need to return applications list in order of application across sweeps. So record the pass name each time it changes something. Applications list is a flat list across all sweeps.\n\nWe need to produce correct output for the given fixtures? Not given expected outputs, but we just implement according to spec.\n\nValidation: If case missing required fields? The problem says \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" But we assume case has exactly text, passes, max_rounds. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nAlso, we should handle case where passes list items might have invalid structure? Probably safe.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) accordingly.\n\nNow we need to output JSON with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string. The source should be valid Python.\n\nWe'll write function:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be dict\")\n    for key in ['text', 'passes', 'max_rounds']:\n        if key not in case:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing key: {key}\")\n    text = case['text']\n    passes = case['passes']\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\n    # validate passes structure\n    if not isinstance(passes, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"passes must be list\")\n    for p in passes:\n        if not isinstance(p, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"each pass must be dict\")\n        for k in ['name', 'old', 'new']:\n            if k not in p:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Pass missing key: {k}\")\n\n    current = text\n    applications = []\n    for round_idx in range(max_rounds):\n        changed_in_round = False\n        for p in passes:\n            old = p['old']\n            new = p['new']\n            if old in current:\n                # replace first occurrence\n                current = current.replace(old, new, 1)\n                applications.append(p['name'])\n                changed_in_round = True\n        if not changed_in_round:\n            return {\n                \"applications\": applications,\n                \"fixed_point\": True,\n                \"text\": current\n            }\n    # After max_rounds, no fixed point\n    return {\n        \"applications\": applications,\n        \"fixed_point\": False,\n        \"text\": current\n    }\n\nNote: The task says \"Return one JSON object with exactly one key, `implementation`.\" So we output that.\n\nWe need to escape the source for JSON string.\n\nLet's produce the final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1314,"completion_tokens":1443,"total_tokens":2757,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1077},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":34},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}